# The Raze device tree only provides Linux extensions (linux/Config.ext.in,
# sourced by Buildroot itself) and Gaia package overrides (packages/, which
# Gaia stages into Buildroot). There are no Buildroot packages of its own;
# the one option below is how lemnos.toml hands Lemnos's users table in.

config BR2_RAZE_LEMNOS_USERS_TABLE
	string "Lemnos users table"
	help
	  A makeusers table whose users the image gets, next to the OS's
	  own BR2_ROOTFS_USERS_TABLES (external.mk adds it to
	  PACKAGES_USERS, so neither replaces the other). lemnos.toml sets
	  it to Lemnos's packaging/buildroot/lemnos-users.table: the
	  `lemnos` user lemnosd.service runs as, created at build time
	  because systemd-sysusers can't add it on a read-only root.
